      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "After 1795, sugarcane became the region’s main crop, with 26,000 acres in the parish producing over $34 million each year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romeville%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Joseph Plantation, a historic sugar plantation, stands as a reminder of Romeville’s plantation‑era heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romeville%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Romeville lies on the Acadian Coast, settled by French‑speaking Acadians between 1756 and 1765 who farmed the fertile riverbanks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
